{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>See, I have called by name.</b> Perhaps it intends to say that they should see a hint of the matter in his name and the names of his ancestors: <b>Betzalel</b> — for he made a shadow (צֵל) for El; <b>son of Uri</b> — for he made a place for Him who is light (אוֹר) to him; <b>son of Hur</b> — for he made Israel free men (בְּנֵי חוֹרִין) from the sin of the calf, as they said of blessed memory (Exodus Rabbah 51:4) on the verse ״מִשְׁכַּן הָעֵדוּת״ — a testimony to all that the sin of the calf was forgiven them. See, the matter is inscribed in his name and the names of his ancestors. And with this the verse's saying <b>va'amalei</b> (and I filled him) with the additional vav comes precisely — to say that besides this, I further add to him a filling of wisdom. And its saying <b>with wisdom</b> (בְּחָכְמָה) rather than saying 'wisdom' (חָכְמָה) — perhaps it alludes in accordance with their words of blessed memory (Berakhot 55a) on the verse (Daniel 2:21) ״יָהֵב חָכְמְתָא לְחַכִּימִין״, that the Holy One, blessed be He, gives wisdom only to one who has wisdom in him, etc.; and this is the verse's saying <b>va'amalei</b> etc. with wisdom — to him who has it I add to fill him with more, and so with understanding etc."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:34:48.904248016Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}